.env
.env.*
# .env.example is the conventional, version-controlled template documenting
# which environment variables this project needs — it is not a real secret,
# and guard_secrets.py/_shared.py specifically allow writing it (with
# content inspection to catch a real key pasted in by mistake). Without
# this negation, the .env.* pattern above ignores it too, silently
# untracking the one file those guards work to keep in git.
!.env.example
*.sqlite3
reports/
staticfiles/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
